{"content-type": "urn:eclecticiq.com:json:3.0", "enrichments": [], "entities": [], "entities_v2": [{"id": "ent_938fe6de", "data": {"title": "Omron NJ501", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_746add86", "data": {"title": "HTTP", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_d1a4f79b", "data": {"title": "Omron R88D-1SN10F-ECT", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_30d35b97", "data": {"title": "Telnet", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_3effffae", "data": {"title": "OMSHELL", "type": "malware"}}, {"id": "ent_ccc02625", "data": {"title": "INCONTROLLER", "type": "intrusion-set"}}, {"id": "ent_e2272cab", "data": {"title": "Omron NX1P2", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_e1271f27", "data": {"title": "Omron FINS", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_dfea9fc8", "data": {"title": "Omron PLCs", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "rep_7cf37921", "data": {"title": "In early 2022, Mandiant, in partnership with Schneider Electric, analyzed a set of novel industrial control system (ICS)-oriented attack tools\u2014which we call INCONTROLLER (aka PIPEDREAM)\u2014built to target machine automation devices", "type": "report", "description": ". The tools can interact with specific industrial equipment embedded in different types of machinery leveraged across multiple industries. \nINCONTROLLER is comprised of three main components:\n TAGRUN\nA tool that scans for OPC servers, enumerates OPC structure/tags, brute forces credentials, and reads/writes OPC tag values.\nCODECALL\nA framework that communicates using Modbus\u2014one of the most common industrial protocols\u2014and Codesys. CODECALL contains modules to interact with, scan, and attack at least three Schneider Electric programmable logic controllers (PLCs).\nOMSHELL\nA framework with capabilities to interact with and scan some types of Omron PLCs via HTTP, Telnet, and Omron FINS protocol. The tool can also interact with Omron's servodrives, which use feedback control to deliver energy to motors for precision motion control.\nOMSHELL is designed to obtain shell access to Omron PLCs, including Omron NX1P2, NJ501, R88D-1SN10F-ECT servo drive, and possibly other similar devices from the NJ/NX product lines. The tool primarily operates using the HTTP protocol, however it also utilizes Omron's proprietary FINS over UDP protocol for scanning and device identification. The framework is modular, which means the attacker can develop and deploy additional capabilities into the tool."}}, {"id": "38a82b7eba70", "data": {"source": "ent_938fe6de", "source_type": "infrastructure", "target": "ent_746add86", "target_type": "infrastructure", "key": "uses", "type": "relation"}, "metadata": {"report_id": "rep_7cf37921"}}, {"id": "a1b3ed57b502", "data": {"source": "ent_938fe6de", "source_type": "infrastructure", "target": "ent_e1271f27", "target_type": "infrastructure", "key": "uses", "type": "relation"}, "metadata": {"report_id": "rep_7cf37921"}}, {"id": "3a2b296a7cd8", "data": {"source": "ent_938fe6de", "source_type": "infrastructure", "target": "ent_30d35b97", "target_type": "infrastructure", "key": "uses", "type": "relation"}, "metadata": {"report_id": "rep_7cf37921"}}, {"id": "89dfff9e0eb0", "data": {"source": "ent_e2272cab", "source_type": "infrastructure", "target": "ent_746add86", "target_type": "infrastructure", "key": "uses", "type": "relation"}, "metadata": {"report_id": "rep_7cf37921"}}, {"id": "a1634c50747d", "data": {"source": "ent_e2272cab", "source_type": "infrastructure", "target": "ent_e1271f27", "target_type": "infrastructure", "key": "uses", "type": "relation"}, "metadata": {"report_id": "rep_7cf37921"}}, {"id": "7c149fdc4abc", "data": {"source": "ent_e2272cab", "source_type": "infrastructure", "target": "ent_30d35b97", "target_type": "infrastructure", "key": "uses", "type": "relation"}, "metadata": {"report_id": "rep_7cf37921"}}, {"id": "5f98ef2c6f82", "data": {"source": "ent_dfea9fc8", "source_type": "infrastructure", "target": "ent_746add86", "target_type": "infrastructure